# Line endings are declared here so a local core.autocrlf setting cannot decide them.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true made Git want CRLF in the working tree while the
# committed blobs and the files the build generates are LF. The result was that
# BmesNgRateStandalone/Services files reported as modified on a clean checkout even though
# `git diff` was empty and the blob hash matched byte for byte — which pollutes `git status`
# for every orchestrated worker and every merge gate that reads it.
#
# LF is what this repository already stores, so this declares the existing convention
# rather than changing it.
* text=auto eol=lf
